1) Government furnished only : Keep first bracketed text and remove the [as indicated].<BRK/>
<BRK/>
2) Contractor supplied only: Keep the second bracketed text.<BRK/>
<BRK/>
3) Combination of Government furnished and Contractor supplied: Keep all bracketed 
text.  When keeping bracketed text (Contractor supplied or combination of Government 
and Contactor supplied) note that computer technology changes quickly and these 
requirements should be edited to reflect current products. Default requirements 
(current as of 2012) have been provided in brackets.</NPR><BRK/>
<AST/><BRK/></NTE>
<BRK/>
<TXT>[The Government will provide the] [Provide a standard desktop computer or a<BRK/>
laptop meeting the following minimum requirements for the] Computer<BRK/>
Workstation Hardware (workstation) [as indicated].</TXT><BRK/>
<BRK/>
<SPT><TTL>Processor</TTL><BRK/>
<BRK/>
<SPT><TTL>Desktop</TTL><BRK/>
